PERCONA: build perl 5.26.3 against libxcrypt's crypt.h (EL8).

glibc's historical struct crypt_data had a current_saltbits member that
perl 5.26 zeroes as a glibc-2.2.5 bug workaround. EL8 ships crypt.h from
libxcrypt, whose struct crypt_data keeps `initialized` for ABI
compatibility but has no current_saltbits, so pp.c fails to compile:
  pp.c:3741: error: 'struct crypt_data' has no member named 'current_saltbits'
Skip the workaround when crypt.h is libxcrypt's (CRYPT_OUTPUT_SIZE is
defined there and not in glibc's crypt.h; EL8's libxcrypt 4.1.1 predates
the XCRYPT_VERSION_NUM macro). Upstream perl dropped this code entirely
in 5.28, and the EL8 distro perl carries the same class of fix; 5.32.1
(EL9) is unaffected.

--- a/pp.c
+++ b/pp.c
@@ -3737,8 +3737,10 @@ PP(pp_crypt)
 #if defined(__GLIBC__) || defined(__EMX__)
 	if (PL_reentrant_buffer->_crypt_struct_buffer) {
 	    PL_reentrant_buffer->_crypt_struct_buffer->initialized = 0;
+#if !defined(CRYPT_OUTPUT_SIZE)
 	    /* work around glibc-2.2.5 bug */
 	    PL_reentrant_buffer->_crypt_struct_buffer->current_saltbits = 0;
+#endif
 	}
 #endif
     }
